🎧 CWPP — 25s Background Music

Target Feel: Intimate, earthy, self-reflective Brazilian indie-folk.
Soft but emotionally grounded. Subtle groove. No bombast.
This is internal truth music — not performance, not drama.

🎼 CONSTRAINT-WEIGHTED PROCEDURAL PROMPT (CWPP)
CORE DNA (LOCKED)

• Tempo: 84–92 BPM (sweet spot ~88 BPM)
• Time Signature: 4/4
• Key Center: E major or C♯ minor relative (warm, introspective tonality)
• Energy Curve: 3 → 5 → 4 (gentle rise, never explosive)
• Duration: 25 seconds
• Function: Background — must support, never dominate

INSTRUMENTATION PALETTE (WEIGHTED)
Primary (High Weight – Always Present)

Nylon-string acoustic guitar (fingerpicked, warm, close mic)
Soft female vocal textures (breathy, layered hums — no full lyrics)
Subtle upright or warm electric bass (rounded tone, minimal attack)
Secondary (Medium Weight – Introduce after 8–10s)
Light brushed percussion (cajón / muted rim taps)
Airy pad (very low in mix, almost felt not heard)
Gentle reverb tail with natural room character
Optional Micro-Details (Low Weight – Sprinkle Sparingly)
Finger slide noises on strings
Soft inhale/exhale vocal artifacts
One reversed guitar swell transition (~18s mark)

STRUCTURE (25s NARRATIVE ARC)
0.00 – 0.07

Intimate Opening
Solo fingerpicked nylon guitar.
Sparse harmony.
Room tone audible.
Let silence breathe between phrases.

0.07 – 0.14

Bass enters quietly.
Soft humming texture layered underneath.
Very light rhythmic pulse begins (subtle, not percussive yet).

0.14 – 0.20

Add brushed percussion — minimal, organic.
Harmony widens slightly (second guitar layer or pad swell).
Emotional lift — not louder, just fuller.

0.20 – 0.23

Micro-moment of suspension:
Brief harmonic shift (relative minor hint).
Tiny reverse swell or vocal breath transition.

0.23 – 0.25

Return to original motif.
Gentle unresolved cadence.
Do not hard resolve — leave emotional openness.

PRODUCTION RULES

❌ No heavy drums
❌ No trap elements
❌ No synthetic arpeggios
❌ No dramatic builds
❌ No EDM-style drops

✅ Organic textures
✅ Analog warmth
✅ Slight tape saturation
✅ Intimate stereo field (not wide cinematic)
✅ Dynamic restraint

EMOTIONAL TARGET

Think:

• Sitting alone after a conversation
• Self-recognition without self-pity
• Quiet strength
• Brazilian sunlight through curtains
• Honest, grounded femininity

If we cross-reference tonal emotional territory, this lives closer to the introspective warmth of tracks like the softness of James Blake (intimate production space) but translated into Brazilian acoustic folk language 

MIXING NOTES

• Vocals slightly forward but airy
• Guitar center-left
• Bass centered, low but warm
• Percussion very low in mix
• Reverb: short room, not hall
• No heavy compression — let dynamics breathe


